      "name": "D2Common_GetRotationValue",
      "signature": "int D2Common_GetRotationValue(uint dwRotationLevel, uint dwBitPattern)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Look up rotation value from table. Validates rotation level in bounds (0-63) and verifies bit pattern has exactly one set bit using bitcount algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwRotationLevel <= 0x3f (64 rotations max)\n2. Call FUN_6fe20aa0(dwBitPattern) to get initial popcount\n3. Validate popcount <= 7 (max 8 bits set for valid patterns)\n4. Verify dwBitPattern has exactly one set bit using Kernighan bitcount:\n   a) Shift and mask: dwBitPattern >> 1,2,3 with masks 0x77777777, 0x33333333, 0x11111111\n   b) Sum and reduce: ((pattern - s1 - s2 - s3) >> 4) - s1 - s2 - s3 + pattern) & 0x0f0f0f0f\n   c) Result % 0xff must equal 1 (popcount validation)\n5. Final popcount via FUN_6fe20aa0(dwBitPattern)\n6. Index lookup table: g_pdwRotationLookupTable[(nFinalBitCount << 6) + dwRotationLevel]\n7. Return dword value from table\n\nParameters:\ndwRotationLevel (uint) - Rotation/direction index, must be 0-63\ndwBitPattern (uint) - Bit pattern to validate and count\n\nReturns:\ndword - Rotation lookup value from g_pdwRotationLookupTable\nCalls FUN_6fe21293(0xffffffff) on validation failure (does not return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Bit pattern must have exactly one set bit (power of 2 representation)\n- Table is 64 x 8 matrix (256 entries, 1024 bytes at g_pdwRotationLookupTable)\n- Ordinal_10023 is assertion/debug output function (logs error then aborts)\n- Function uses register-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3f = 63 decimal (max rotation level)\n0x40 = 64 decimal (stride for next rotation in lookup)\n0x77777777, 0x33333333, 0x11111111 = Kernighan bit counting masks\n0x0f0f0f0f = Final bitcount reduction mask\n0xff = 255 decimal (modulo for bitcount validation)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:da2f4223bacbd2e9124c08b11e4d0efe",
