      "name": "CELFILE_AddImageFrameToCel",
      "signature": "void CELFILE_AddImageFrameToCel(dword dwCelKey, byte * pbImageData, dword dwImageByteStride, dword dwPixelWidth, dword dwPixelHeight, dword dwUserParam1, dword dwUserParam2, dword dwUserParam3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Adds an image frame to a cel/sprite entry in the cel data hash table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwPixelWidth and dwPixelHeight are non-zero (assert on failure)\n2. Validate dwImageByteStride >= dwPixelHeight (assert on failure)\n3. Enter g_CelCriticalSection for thread-safe access\n4. Compute hash bucket index: g_dwCelTableMask & dwCelKey\n5. Look up cel entry in g_pCelDataTable at bucket * 0xC offset\n6. Search linked list for matching dwCelKey\n7. If no match found, leave critical section early (iVar3 = 0)\n8. If match found, create new frame node via InsertListNodeLinked\n9. Increment frame count at pCelEntry[9]\n10. Store frame metadata in new node:\n    - Offset +0x10: dwPixelWidth\n    - Offset +0x14: dwPixelWidth * dwPixelHeight (total pixels)\n    - Offset +0x0C: dwPixelHeight\n    - Offset +0x18: dwUserParam1\n    - Offset +0x1C: dwUserParam2\n    - Offset +0x08: dwUserParam3\n11. Check RGB mode flag (pCelEntry[6] & 0x4): if set, multiply height by 3\n12. Allocate destination buffer via FogMemAlloc(width * height)\n13. Store buffer pointer at frame node +0x20\n14. Copy image data via CopyMemoryWithStride with stride support\n15. If search was successful (iVar3 != 0), leave critical section\n\nParameters:\n  dwCelKey         - Hash key identifying the cel entry in table\n  pbImageData      - Source image pixel data buffer\n  dwImageByteStride - Byte stride/pitch of source image (row width in bytes)\n  dwPixelWidth     - Width of image in pixels\n  dwPixelHeight    - Height of image in pixels/rows\n  dwUserParam1     - User-defined parameter stored at frame +0x18\n  dwUserParam2     - User-defined parameter stored at frame +0x1C\n  dwUserParam3     - User-defined parameter stored at frame +0x08\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - RGB mode (flag 0x4): Height multiplied by 3 for RGB channel separation\n  - Hash collision: Searches linked list for exact dwCelKey match\n  - Missing entry: Leaves critical section without adding frame\n\nStructure Layout (Cel Entry, 0xC byte stride):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  +0x00   4     dwKey         Cel key identifier\n  +0x04   4     pNext         Next entry in collision chain\n  +0x08   4     pFrameList    Pointer to frame linked list\n\nStructure Layout (Frame Node):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  +0x08   4     dwUserParam3  User parameter 3\n  +0x0C   4     dwPixelHeight Pixel height\n  +0x10   4     dwPixelWidth  Pixel width\n  +0x14   4     dwTotalPixels Width * Height\n  +0x18   4     dwUserParam1  User parameter 1\n  +0x1C   4     dwUserParam2  User parameter 2\n  +0x20   4     pbPixelData   Allocated pixel buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x217 - Assert line for dimension validation\n  0x218 - Assert line for stride validation\n  0x227 - Line number for FogMemAlloc call\n  0x4   - RGB mode flag in cel entry flags\n  0xC   - Stride of cel table entries (12 bytes)\n  0x2C  - Offset to frame list in cel entry (pThis + 0xB dwords)",
