      "name": "DecodeCelFrame",
      "signature": "void DecodeCelFrame(int * pCelFile, int nBufferOffset, int nY, void * pRGB, void * pAlpha, void * pDestSurface, int nHeight, uint dwTranslationOffset, uint dwFrameIndex, void * pOutputBuffer, int nYOffset, int nHeightClamp, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decode and render a CEL frame to destination surface with coordinate/height validation and optional transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pCelFile pointer and check dwVersion == 6\n2. Validate dwFlags & 0x4 == 0\n3. Validate pDestSurface != NULL\n4. Load pCelFile.dwData and validate != NULL\n5. Calculate nFrameYEnd = nY + pCelFile.dwCelHeight\n6. Calculate nClipStartY = nFrameYEnd - nYOffset, nClipEndY = nClipStartY - nHeightClamp\n7. Clamp Y values: if nClipStartY < 0 set to 0; if nClipEndY >= nHeight set to nHeight - 1\n8. Calculate render height = nClipEndY - nClipStartY (skip if <= 0)\n9. Lookup decoder function from table using pCelFile.dwFormat as index\n10. Validate decoder != NULL\n11. Call decoder with frame offset, stride, height, and format parameters\n\nParameters:\n  pCelFile (int *) - Pointer to CELFILE structure with version, flags, format, width, height, data\n  nBufferOffset (int) - Byte offset into frame data\n  nY (int) - Y coordinate for frame placement\n  pRGB (void *) - RGB palette or color translation buffer\n  pAlpha (void *) - Alpha/transparency buffer\n  pDestSurface (void *) - Destination surface pointer (must not be NULL)\n  nHeight (int) - Height limit for clipping\n  dwTranslationOffset (uint) - Offset within translation table\n  dwFrameIndex (uint) - Frame index selector\n  pOutputBuffer (void *) - Output/intermediate buffer for decoded frame data\n  nYOffset (int) - Y offset for vertical positioning\n  nHeightClamp (int) - Height clamp value\n  dwFlags (uint) - Format/behavior flags (bit 0x4 validated)\n\nReturns:\n  void (always succeeds or terminates with assertion failure on invalid input)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
