      "comment": "Validates pointer and returns field value at offset 0x10.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameter pData from stack [ESP + 0x4]\n2. Test pData for NULL value\n3. If pData is NULL (zero), trigger fatal error:\n   - Push error code 0x587\n   - Push error message string pointer (0x6fe2e094)\n   - Push global error context (0x6fe2e3d8)\n   - Call Ordinal_10023 (Fog.ErrorMsg) to display error\n   - Call FUN_6fe21293(0xffffffff) to terminate\n4. If pData is valid (non-NULL):\n   - Load DWORD from [pData + 0x10]\n   - Return value in EAX\n5. Stack cleanup: Caller pops 4-byte parameter\n\nParameters:\n  pData (void *) - Pointer to structure; must be non-NULL or function terminates\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Value at offset 0x10 of pData structure (success)\n  Does not return if pData is NULL (calls exit handler)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer triggers fatal error with code 0x587\n  - Error message reference: s_C__Projects_Diablo2_Source_D2CMP_6fe2e094\n  - Function never returns if validation fails\n  - Assumes 4-byte aligned DWORD field at offset 0x10\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - Ordinal_10023 - Fog.ErrorMsg (error reporting)\n  - FUN_6fe21293 - Exit/termination handler",
