      "name": "DestroyGameDataObject",
      "signature": "void DestroyGameDataObject(GameData * pGameData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destroy game data object and perform complete cleanup operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fadc310 to clean up internal chain data structures\n2. Save ESI register and load game data pointer\n3. Set ECX register for __fastcall convention to FUN_6fadc310\n4. Call Ordinal_403 destructor with AUSGAMEDATA class identifier\n5. Push parameters in reverse order: 0, -2 (destroy mode), string, object\n6. Restore ESI register and return with stack cleanup\n\nParameters:\npGameData (GameData*): Pointer to game data object structure containing chain pointers and offsets\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function does not return a value, performs cleanup operations only\n\nSpecial Cases:\nDestruction sequence is critical - internal cleanup must occur before final destructor call\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xfffffffe (-2): Destruction mode flag passed to Ordinal_403 indicating object destruction\n0x00000000: Final parameter for cleanup operation, likely completion status\n\".?AUSGAMEDATA@@\": Mangled C++ class name identifier for game data object type used by destructor\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwField0       | uint  | First structure field\n0x04   | 4    | pFirstChain    | void* | Pointer to first cleanup chain\n0x08   | 4    | dwFirstOffset  | uint  | Offset for first chain operations  \n0x0C   | 4    | pSecondChain   | void* | Pointer to second cleanup chain\n0x10   | 4    | dwSecondOffset | uint  | Offset for second chain operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
