      "name": "DestroyListManager",
      "signature": "void DestroyListManager(int * pListMgr)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destroys a list manager, cleaning up all nodes and freeing bucket array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear state field at +0x10\n2. Extract all nodes from linked list via ExtractListNode (loop while +0x0C > 0)\n3. For each bucket in array (+0x1C): unlink nodes from internal chain\n4. Clear state fields (+0x10, +0x24)\n5. Destroy each bucket node via DestroyNodeWithCleanup\n6. Free bucket array via Ordinal_403 if non-null\n7. Zero capacity/count/array fields (+0x14, +0x18, +0x1C)\n\nParameters:\n- pListMgr (int*): Pointer to list manager structure\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout (ListMgr):\nOffset | Field        | Description\n0x04   | pListData    | Pointer to list data\n0x0C   | nTailOffset  | Tail offset/count for extraction\n0x10   | nState1      | State flag (cleared during destroy)\n0x14   | nCapacity    | Capacity (cleared at end)\n0x18   | nBucketCount | Number of buckets in array\n0x1C   | pBuckets     | Pointer to bucket array (12-byte stride)\n0x24   | nState2      | Secondary state (cleared during destroy)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0C (12): Bucket structure stride\n- -0x2: Flag passed to Ordinal_403",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
