      "name": "UnlinkGameDataFromCollections",
      "signature": "void UnlinkGameDataFromCollections(GameDataObjectWithCollections * pGameDataObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes a game data object from two linked list collections during cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if second collection pointer (offset 0xc) is valid\n2. If valid, extract collection offset (offset 0x10) for pointer arithmetic\n3. If offset is negative, use bitwise NOT as direct pointer address\n4. Otherwise, calculate target pointer using base + (offset - node_backlink)\n5. Update collection linkage by storing node pointer at calculated address  \n6. Clear node's collection pointer (offset 0xc) and offset (offset 0x10)\n7. Repeat same process for first collection using offsets 0x4 and 0x8\n8. Clear first collection pointer and offset values\n\nParameters:\n  pGameDataObject (GameDataObjectWithCollections *): Pointer to game data object containing collection references\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Negative offset values (0x80000000+) indicate absolute pointer addresses\n  - Uses bitwise NOT (~offset) to convert negative offsets to pointers\n  - Safe to call with NULL pointers - function checks before unlinking\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name         | Type | Description\n  -------|------|-------------------|------|------------------------------------------  \n  0x00   | 4    | field0            | ptr  | (not accessed by this function)\n  0x04   | 4    | pFirstCollection  | ptr  | First collection node pointer\n  0x08   | 4    | dwFirstOffset     | uint | Offset for first collection linkage\n  0x0C   | 4    | pSecondCollection | ptr  | Second collection node pointer  \n  0x10   | 4    | dwSecondOffset    | uint | Offset for second collection linkage\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x04 - Node backlink offset within collection entries\n  0x80000000 - Negative offset threshold for absolute addressing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0e8a163b1dfdc9385e2bd41b7e5e057d",
