      "name": "InitializeGameDataElementChains",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameDataElementChains(GameDataElement * pGameDataElement)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize GameDataElement with security pointer chains for integrity validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate pointer to element data field at offset +0x4\n2. Store self-referencing pointer at +0x4 (points to itself for chain validation)\n3. Store bitwise inverted pointer at +0x8 (security check value)\n\nParameters:\npGameDataElement - Pointer to GameDataElement structure to initialize\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPointer chain setup provides integrity checking mechanism\nBitwise NOT at +0x8 serves as validation signature against corruption\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4 - Offset to first pointer field in GameDataElement\n0x8 - Offset to validation pointer field in GameDataElement\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type    | Description\n+0x00  | 4    | dwValue        | uint    | Element data value\n+0x04  | 4    | pSelfPtr       | uint    | Self-referencing pointer for chain validation\n+0x08  | 4    | dwValidation   | uint    | Bitwise NOT of pSelfPtr for integrity check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c44ae1e162c2930cd758a6126855d763",
