      "name": "ProcessCelDirectionFrames",
      "signature": "uint ProcessCelDirectionFrames(uint dwCelData, uint dwCelOutput)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes CEL animation frames and organizes them by direction/rotation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input flags (assert if CELFILE_24BIT flag set at offset 0x18)\n2. Calculate frames per direction from total (0x24) / direction count (0x28)\n3. Iterate through linked list of frame data nodes at offset 0x34\n4. For each node: call CompressItemDataLine to compress data\n5. Allocate 0x82-byte frame buffer via AllocClientMemory\n6. Copy node fields (0x8-0x1c) and compressed data to frame buffer\n7. Call UpdatePaletteIndex with operation 0x8d\n8. Calculate rotation index via GetRotationLookupValue\n9. Store frame pointer in output array at [direction][frame] slot\n\nParameters:\n- dwCelData (uint): Pointer to CEL file data structure\n- dwCelOutput (uint): Pointer to output CEL structure for direction frames\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Last calculated direction index (frameIdx / framesPerDir)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x82 (130): Size of allocated frame buffer\n- 0x8d (141): Palette update operation code\n- 0x18: Frame pointer array offset in output structure\n- 0x24: Total frame count offset in CEL data\n- 0x28: Direction count offset in CEL data\n- 0x34: Linked list head offset in CEL data",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:cb076e6de095fbae651536ebd8f4d683",
