      "name": "CompressItemDataLine",
      "signature": "int CompressItemDataLine(byte * pbSrcData, int nLineStride, uint dwLineCount, byte * pbAlign, byte * * ppCompressed, int * pnCompressedSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Compress item data line with run-length encoding. Processes source pixel data row-wise, encoding transparent (zero) and non-transparent runs separately.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate compression output buffer via Ordinal_10042 (D2Common.GetItemData)\n2. Determine stride direction based on alignment flag (pbAlign LSB): normal or reverse\n3. For each source line (nLineCount iterations):\n   a. Check if current pixel is transparent (zero)\n   b. If transparent: Count run length via CountAndValidateRunLength(), encode as (length | 0x80) if valid\n   c. If non-transparent: Count run via FUN_6fe16060(), encode length then copy pixel values\n   d. On validation error: Encode marker (0x80) and skip to next line\n4. Store final output pointer in ppCompressed, write total compressed size to pnCompressedSize\n\nParameters:\npbSrcData (byte *) - Source pixel data, first line location (may be adjusted based on alignment)\nnLineStride (int) - Bytes between consecutive lines (positive normal, negative reverse)\nnLineCount (uint) - Number of lines to compress\npbAlign (byte *) - Alignment flag (LSB: 0=normal direction, 1=reverse)\nppCompressed (byte **) - Output: pointer to allocated compression buffer\npnCompressedSize (int *) - Output: total bytes written to compressed buffer\n\nReturns:\nint - Final count (appears to be total line count processed or status indicator)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x80 - Run-length encoding marker for transparent/skip runs\n0x7f - Maximum run length value (127 pixels max per run)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Reverse processing: stride negated, starting address adjusted to line end\n- Validation failure (local_8 or local_c non-zero): Emits 0x80 marker and advances line\n- Zero line count: Returns without processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:7fb1a9cb96d4e9e4923a111193846a7b",
