      "name": "FindTileInHashTable",
      "signature": "int FindTileInHashTable(void * * pHashTable, dword * pOutputBuffer, dword nMaxCount, int nTileY, int nTileX, int nLevel)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Search hash table for tile matching coordinates and return linked list count\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pHashTable pointer not NULL (assert if invalid)\n2. Validate pOutputBuffer pointer not NULL (assert if invalid)\n3. Return 0 if nMaxCount is zero\n4. Calculate hash key: byHashKey = (nLevel * 2 - nTileY) + nTileX, mask to 0x7f\n5. Assert hash key is valid (byHashKey < 0x7f)\n6. Get hash bucket entry from table[byHashKey * 4]\n7. Search linked list of bucket entries:\n   - Compare entry[1] == nLevel, entry[0] == nTileX, entry[2] == nTileY\n   - If all match, found = true and proceed to copy\n   - Otherwise follow entry[4] pointer to next bucket entry\n8. If found, copy data list starting at entry[3]:\n   - For each node in list (up to nMaxCount):\n     - Copy node[0] to output buffer\n     - Move to node[4] (next node)\n     - Increment nItemCount\n9. Return nItemCount (number of items copied)\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTable (void **): Hash table base pointer (array of bucket entry pointers)\n- pOutputBuffer (dword *): Output buffer for copying tile data\n- nMaxCount (dword): Maximum number of items to copy\n- nTileY (int): Tile Y coordinate for lookup key\n- nTileX (int): Tile X coordinate for lookup key\n- nLevel (int): Tile level for lookup key\n\nReturns:\n- int: Number of items copied to output buffer (0 if not found or nMaxCount is 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts if pHashTable or pOutputBuffer NULL\n- Asserts if calculated hash key exceeds 0x7f limit\n- Returns 0 if nMaxCount is 0\n- Returns 0 if no hash bucket entry matches coordinates\n- Stops copying when linked list exhausted or nMaxCount limit reached\n- Note: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away by compiler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x02: Multiplier for nLevel in hash calculation\n- 0x7f: Hash table size (128 buckets)\n- 0x04: Entry stride in hash table and field offsets\n- 0x10: Offset to next bucket entry pointer\n- 0x0c: Offset to data list head pointer\n- 0xcf, 0xd0, 0x1e: Line numbers in assertion failures\n\nHash Bucket Entry Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | nTileX     | dword| Tile X coordinate\n0x04   | 4    | nLevel     | dword| Tile level\n0x08   | 4    | nTileY     | dword| Tile Y coordinate\n0x0c   | 4    | pDataList  | void*| Pointer to linked list of tile data\n0x10   | 4    | pNextEntry | void*| Pointer to next bucket entry in collision chain\n\nData List Node Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwData     | dword| Tile data value\n0x04   | 4    | pNextNode  | void*| Pointer to next node in list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
