      "name": "LoadPaletteFromFile",
      "signature": "dword LoadPaletteFromFile(char * lpszFilePath, int nStartEntry, int nEndEntry)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Load palette from standard 768-byte file or legacy PAL header format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: lpszFilePath != NULL, 0 <= nStartEntry <= nEndEntry <= 0xFF (assert on failure)\n2. Store nEndEntry into g_dwPaletteEndIndex; set g_dwPaletteStartIndex=1\n3. Build distance lookup table: loop from -256 to 0, store i*i into g_anPaletteDistanceLookup[i+256]\n4. Get length of lpszFilePath via lstrlenA\n5. If length == 0: initialize g_paPaletteTable with bytes 0-255, set g_dwPaletteValidFlag=1, return 1\n6. CreateFileA(lpszFilePath, 0x80000000, 1, NULL, 3, 0, NULL) - open file for reading\n7. If INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE: output 3 debug strings (error, path, newline), return 0\n8. GetFileSize(hFile) - check if standard 0x300 (768) bytes\n9. If size == 0x300: standard palette\n   - ReadFile into g_abPaletteData at offset 0x300 bytes\n   - If read 0x300 bytes: copy to g_paPaletteTable via byte-swapping loop, set flag=1, close, return 1\n   - Else: set flag=0, close, return 0\n10. Else: legacy format with header\n   - Close handle, reopen same file\n   - If INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE: same error output, return 0\n   - Clear 0x80 bytes (0x20 dwords) to zero at [ESP+0x1C]\n   - ReadFile first 0x80 bytes into cStack_384\n   - Validate header: bytes[0]==0x0A, bytes[1]==0x05, bytes[3]==0x08\n   - If valid: clear 0x301-byte buffer (acStack_304)\n     * SetFilePointer(hFile, -0x301, NULL, 2) - seek to end-0x301\n     * ReadFile final 0x301 bytes into acStack_304\n     * If read 0x301 bytes AND acStack_304[0]==0x0C: copy palette via 3-byte stride, return 1\n     * Else: output \"Unable to extract palette...\" error, return 0\n   - Else: output \"File is not valid 256-color...\" error, return 0\n11. On any error path: set g_dwPaletteValidFlag=0, close handle, return 0\n\nParameters:\nlpszFilePath - File path to load (ASSERT if NULL); supports relative/absolute paths\nnStartEntry - Palette start index, must be 0-255 (ASSERT on violation)\nnEndEntry - Palette end index, must be 0-255 and >= nStartEntry (ASSERT on violation)\n\nReturns:\n1 (success) - palette loaded and initialized, g_dwPaletteValidFlag set\n0 (failure) - file error, validation failed, or read failed; g_dwPaletteValidFlag cleared\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x300 - Standard palette size (256 colors * 3 bytes RGB = 768 bytes)\n0x80 - Header size for legacy format (128 bytes)\n0x301 - Legacy palette size with trailer (768 + 1 byte trailer)\n0x0A, 0x05, 0x08 - Legacy PAL header magic bytes [0], [1], [3]\n0x0C - Legacy palette trailer marker (form feed char)\n-0x256 to 0 - Distance lookup table range for color matching\n0x80000000 - GENERIC_READ flag for CreateFileA",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:fb91665bf401004261cec7ea9e4a0692",
