      "name": "FreeGouraudTableMemory",
      "signature": "void FreeGouraudTableMemory(void * pMemory)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Deallocates Gouraud shading table memory via VirtualFree.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call VirtualFree with pMemory pointer\n2. Use MEM_RELEASE flag (0x8000) for deallocation\n3. dwSize parameter set to 0 (required for MEM_RELEASE)\n4. Return void (no error checking)\n\nParameters:\npMemory (void*) - Pointer to Gouraud table memory allocated by CreateGouraudTables (ECX in __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; relies on caller (CleanupGouraudTables) for error handling\n\nSpecial Cases:\nCalled multiple times by CleanupGouraudTables to free separate table allocations (X, Y, XVal, Subtile, Tile)\nAssumes pMemory was allocated via VirtualAlloc from same heap\nNo validation of memory pointer - relies on valid allocation state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8000 (MEM_RELEASE) - VirtualFree flag to decommit and release memory region\n0x0 - dwSize parameter (must be 0 with MEM_RELEASE)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
