      "name": "DestructorWithCleanup",
      "signature": "void DestructorWithCleanup(ObjectWithCallback * pObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destructor for object with optional cleanup callback\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set vtable pointer at object offset 0 to type_info::vftable for RTTI\n2. Call FUN_6fb9b69c(0x1b) to perform first cleanup phase\n3. Load callback pointer from object offset 4 into ESI register\n4. Test ESI against zero using TEST instruction\n5. If callback is NULL (zero), skip callback invocation and proceed to final cleanup\n6. If callback is non-NULL, invoke FUN_6fb9b712 with callback pointer as parameter\n7. Call FUN_6fb9b6fd(0x1b) to perform final cleanup phase\n8. Return void\n\nParameters:\npObject (ObjectWithCallback *) - Pointer to object instance containing vftable and optional callback pointer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns after cleanup operations complete\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Callback pointer at offset +4 may be NULL, cleanup is conditionally invoked\n- Magic value 0x1b passed to both cleanup phases indicates resource type or phase identifier",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
