      "comment": "Structured Exception Handling (SEH) filter dispatcher that evaluates exceptions and coordinates unwind handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exception flags from EXCEPTION_RECORD.ExceptionFlags (offset +0x4)\n2. Mask with 0x66 to check for continuation/nested exception flags\n3. If continuation flags set: Mark context.dwState[0x24] = 1 (filter consumed) and return 1 (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER)\n4. If continuation flags clear: Call FUN_6fb9b884 (exception processor) with exception record and context fields\n5. Check if context.dwState[0x24] still == 0 (filter pending)\n6. If pending (0), call ExceptionUnwindHandler(pContext, pExceptionRecord) to manage stack unwinding\n7. Extract and invoke exception handler continuation function pointer at context.pHandlerFunc[0x18]\n8. Return handler result code to SEH dispatcher\n\nParameters:\npExceptionRecord - PEXCEPTION_RECORD: Exception information (ExceptionCode, ExceptionFlags, ExceptionRecord chain)\npContext - SEH_CONTEXT*: Opaque SEH context structure containing handler state and function pointers (offsets: 0x8=pParam1, 0xc=pParam2, 0x10=dwParam3, 0x14=pParam4, 0x18=pHandlerFunc, 0x1c=dwSavedESP, 0x20=dwSavedEBP, 0x24=dwState)\ndwContext - DWORD: Context identifier/flags passed to exception processor\n\nReturns:\n1 (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) - Filter consumed exception, continue handler\nHandler-specific value - Result from continuation function at context.pHandlerFunc[0x18] (stored in EAX return register)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exception flags 0x66 (EH_UNWINDING | EH_EXIT_UNWIND) indicate cleanup/nested exception - fast-path return\n- Offset 0x24 in context acts as filter state: 1=consumed, 0=pending unwind\n- Indirect function call at offset 0x18 allows handler-specific continuation logic\n- Return value from indirect call stored in EAX (SSA temporary, not visible in decompiled locals)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x66 - Exception flags mask for unwinding bits (0x02 EH_UNWINDING | 0x04 EH_EXIT_UNWIND | 0x60 reserved continuation bits)\n0x24 - Context offset for filter state flag (DWORD)\n0x18 - Context offset for handler continuation function pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
