      "name": "CppExceptionFilter",
      "signature": "void CppExceptionFilter(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord, PVOID pContext, DWORD dwDispatcherContext, uint dwExceptionFlag, uint dwRangeTable, char chContinue, int nRangeIndex, PVOID pFrameInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "C++ exception filter for structured exception handling and unwind processing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate slot address from context against range table bounds\n2. Check if exception code is 0xe06d7363 (C++ exception) with 3 parameters\n3. If standard C++ exception signature detected, retrieve unwind handler from thread-local data\n4. Call exception validation function to verify handler state\n5. Search range table for slot address match using SearchRangeTable\n6. Iterate through matching range entries comparing slot address against ranges\n7. For matching range, iterate through handler count and handler list entries\n8. Call handler comparison function for each handler entry to find matching handler\n9. If match found, invoke exception handler (FUN_6fb9bc8d) with parameters\n10. If no range match or continue flag set, dispatch to alternative handler (FUN_6fb9bad2)\n\nParameters:\nPEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord - Exception information (code, parameters)\nPVOID pContext - Context structure containing slot address at offset 0x8\nDWORD dwDispatcherContext - Dispatcher context value\nuint dwExceptionFlag - Exception processing flags\nuint dwRangeTable - Pointer to range table for handler lookup\nchar chContinue - Continue/stop flag (0=stop at first match, nonzero=continue to alternatives)\nint nRangeIndex - Exception index for range table search\nPVOID pFrameInfo - Frame information structure\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value, exception handling state modified via function calls)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Slot address -1 is invalid and triggers error\n- Slot address >= range table size is invalid\n- 0xe06d7363 with different parameter counts handled as non-C++ exception\n- ExceptionInformation[2] == 0 indicates special handler case\n- Handler count of 0 in range entry skips handler iteration\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xe06d7363 - C++ exception code (VCppException magic signature)\n0x19930520 - C++ exception parameter signature validation value\n0xffffff00 - Mask for exception flag byte (preserves high 24 bits)\n0x10 - Handler entry size (16 bytes per handler block)\n0x6c, 0x70 - Offsets into thread-local data for exception handler retrieval\n\nNote: Function uses SSA temporaries optimized away (pDVar1, extraout_var)",
