      "name": "FormatFloatingPointDigits",
      "signature": "void FormatFloatingPointDigits(char * szOutputBuffer, int nDigitCount, FloatFormatState * pFormatState)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats floating-point digit string with optional rounding and exponent adjustment\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer with leading zero ('0') \n2. Copy source digits from format state to output buffer, padding with zeros\n3. Null-terminate the digit string\n4. Apply rounding if next source digit >= '5' by incrementing from right\n5. Handle carry propagation through consecutive '9' digits  \n6. Adjust exponent if first digit becomes '1' after rounding\n7. Shift digits left if no leading '1' to normalize output\n\nParameters:\n  szOutputBuffer - Output buffer to receive formatted digit string\n  nDigitCount - Number of significant digits to format\n  pFormatState - Pointer to FloatFormatState structure\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results stored in szOutputBuffer and pFormatState->nExponent updated\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nDigitCount <= 0, outputs single '0' and null terminator\n  - Source digit exhaustion fills remainder with '0' characters  \n  - Rounding '999...9' propagates carry to create leading '1' \n  - Leading '1' after rounding increments exponent and shifts digits\n\nStructure Layout:\n  FloatFormatState (16 bytes):\n    Offset  Size  Field Name     Type     Description\n    0x00    4     dwReserved     uint     Reserved field \n    0x04    4     nExponent      int      Current exponent value\n    0x08    4     dwReserved2    uint     Reserved field\n    0x0C    4     szDigits       char*    Source digit string pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:ea3677ef9e925b399045d64b19f6ab3e",
