      "name": "DestroyGameObjectWithMembers",
      "signature": "void DestroyGameObjectWithMembers(void * pGameObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destructor for game object with exception-safe member cleanup using SEH.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Install Structured Exception Handling (SEH) frame by pushing handler address and marker\n2. Save current FS:[0] exception list pointer to restore later\n3. Update FS:[0] to point to new exception handler frame\n4. Set object's vtable pointer to UnlinkListNode (0x6fc36ad4)\n5. Initialize destructionState to 2 (cleanup phase)\n6. Call DestroyResourceCollections() to clean up resource management lists\n7. Transition destructionState to 1 before member cleanup\n8. Call UnwindExceptionList() on member at offset +0x38 with exception safety\n9. Transition destructionState to 0 as second member is about to be cleaned\n10. Call UnwindExceptionList() on member at offset +0x28 for secondary cleanup\n11. Mark destructionState as -1 (completion marker) for exception handler visibility\n12. Call InitializeAURGNDestructor() for final object-level cleanup\n13. Restore previous exception list pointer from FS:[0]\n14. Clean up stack frame (ADD ESP, 0x10)\n15. Return with RET 0x4 (caller cleanup of parameter)\n\nParameters:\n- pGameObject: Pointer to game object structure with:\n  * Offset +0x0: Virtual function table pointer (set to UnlinkListNode)\n  * Offset +0x28: First member requiring cleanup (called via UnwindExceptionList)\n  * Offset +0x38: Second member requiring cleanup (called via UnwindExceptionList)\n\nReturns:\nNone (void). Function uses RET 0x4 to clean up the 4-byte parameter pushed by caller.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exception handling uses Windows SEH mechanism via FS:[0] (Thread Information Block)\n- destructionState field is monitored by exception handler for cleanup progress tracking\n- Members are destructed in reverse order: +0x38 first, then +0x28\n- If exception occurs during cleanup, exception handler uses destructionState to resume\n- RET 0x4 indicates this is a __stdcall function where caller cleanup is performed by callee\n\nStructure Layout (pGameObject at *EDI):\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type      Description\n------  ----  -----------------  --------  ----------------------------\n+0x0    4     vftable            void*     Virtual function table pointer\n+0x28   4     memberDestructor1  void*     First member with destructor\n+0x38   4     memberDestructor2  void*     Second member with destructor",
