      "signature": "void ProcessMemberDestructors(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Iterates through array of member objects and invokes destructor on each element\n\nProcesses an array of member objects by invoking a destructor function on each\nelement in sequence, then optionally calls a cleanup/deallocation function after\nall elements have been processed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI and EDI registers for use as working registers\n2. Load element count from pObjectStructure+0x4 into EAX\n3. Test count for zero; if empty or non-positive, skip to cleanup phase (JBE)\n4. Save EBX register for use as offset accumulator\n5. Clear EDI to zero as loop counter initialization\n6. Clear EBX to zero as offset counter (stride accumulator)\n7. Load base pointer of member array from pObjectStructure+0x8 into EAX\n8. For each element in array (while loopCounter < elementCount):\n   a. Calculate element address as (arrayBase + elementOffsetAccumulator)\n   b. Push calculated element address onto stack as parameter\n   c. Call ExecuteWithExceptionHandler(elementAddress) to invoke destructor\n   d. Reload element count from pObjectStructure+0x4 for loop check\n   e. Increment loop counter (EDI) by 1\n   f. Advance offset accumulator by 0xC (12 bytes - element stride)\n   g. Compare loopCounter against elementCount using CMP\n   h. Jump to loop_start_process_element if loopCounter < elementCount (JC)\n9. Restore EBX from stack after loop completion\n10. Load cleanup function pointer from pObjectStructure+0x8\n11. Test cleanup pointer for null\n12. If cleanup pointer is non-null:\n    a. Push parameter 0x0 (error code)\n    b. Push parameter -0x2 (error status)\n    c. Push context pointer 0x6fc41bc0 (g_szTSExplicitListURGNTypeDescriptor)\n    d. Push cleanup function pointer as first argument\n    e. Call function at 0x6fc0b960 (error handler with cleanup semantics)\n13. Restore EDI and ESI from stack\n14. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npObjectStructure (void *): Pointer to member container structure containing:\n  - Offset +0x4: DWORD element count (number of members)\n  - Offset +0x8: DWORD pointer to member array (each element 0xC/12 bytes)\n               OR cleanup/deallocation function pointer (reuses same offset)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns control to caller after processing complete\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty container: If element count is 0 or negative, loop is skipped (JBE\n  condition) and function proceeds directly to cleanup phase\n- Array stride: Fixed at 0xC (12) bytes per element - calculated using\n  repeated ADD EBX,0xc operations\n- Cleanup handler optional: Null pointer check (TEST ESI,ESI / JZ) prevents\n  calling cleanup if pointer is null\n- Register preservation: Function preserves ESI, EDI, EBX across execution\n- Parameter reuse: Offset +0x8 serves dual purpose: initially array base\n  pointer for loop iteration, then reload as cleanup function pointer after\n  loop completes - suggests struct layout: [0x0]=reserved, [0x4]=count,\n  [0x8]=arrayOrCleanupPtr\n- Exception handling: All destructor calls wrapped in ExecuteWithExceptionHandler\n  to handle potential exceptions during member destruction\n- Cleanup context: Cleanup function invoked with error context parameters\n  (0x0, -0x2, g_szTSExplicitListURGNTypeDescriptor) suggesting error handler\n  integration and exception unwinding scenario",
