      "name": "UnwindExceptionList",
      "signature": "void UnwindExceptionList(int * exceptObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Unwinds and restores exception handling state when exiting protected regions.\n\nThis function manages the structured exception handling (SEH) cleanup chain by\nremoving the current exception handler context from the thread-local exception\nlist and restoring the previous exception handler state. It handles linked list\nmanipulation with both direct pointer values and calculated offsets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current exception state (FS:[0] contains exception chain head)\n2. Install exception handler frame onto the exception chain\n3. Call exception cleanup routine (UnlinkAndClearListNodes) to process pending handlers\n4. Load node pointer from exceptObject+4 (the linked list node to unwind)\n5. If node pointer is non-null:\n   a. Load offset value from exceptObject+8\n   b. If offset is negative (TEST EDX, EDX; JGE):\n      - Use bitwise complement: targetPointer = ~offsetValue\n   c. If offset is non-negative:\n      - Calculate target: targetPointer = (nodePointerLocation + offsetValue - node[+4])\n      - This adjusts offset by the node's successor pointer\n   d. Store node pointer at target location: *targetPointer = nodePointer\n   e. Link successor: node[+4] = offsetValue (establish backward link)\n   f. Clear node pointer and offset fields in exceptObject\n6. Restore exception chain head (FS:[0]) from saved context\n7. Clean up stack frame and return with RET 0x4 (stdcall callee cleanup)\n\nParameters:\n- exceptObject: Pointer to exception context structure containing linked list state\n\nReturns:\n- void; modifies exception chain and linked list structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type       Description\n0       4     handler          void*      Exception handler frame (FS:[0])\n4       4     nodePointer      int*       Linked list node to unwind\n8       4     offsetValue      uint       Offset or complement value for target calc\n12      4     savedMarker      uint       Saved exception marker (0 on entry)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative offset values use complement form (~offset) for direct pointer access\n- Positive offset values require pointer arithmetic through linked list\n- Function manages C++ exception unwinding during stack destruction\n- Part of structured exception handling (SEH) framework for cleanup handlers",
