      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.11": 127,
        "LoD/1.11b": 127,
        "LoD/1.12a": 127,
        "LoD/1.13c": 127,
        "LoD/1.13d": 127
      },
      "name": "ProcessEntityPoolSlots",
      "signature": "int ProcessEntityPoolSlots(void * pEntityManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes entity pool slots for overflow management and mask validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read entity pool mask from pEntityManager[+0x24]\n2. If mask exceeds 0x3FF (1023), return 0 indicating valid state\n3. Load current slot index from pEntityManager[+0x10]\n4. If slot index < 4, reset to 0; otherwise subtract 3\n5. Calculate slot base offset: index * 12 bytes (3 dwords)\n6. Load slot value from entity array at offset +0x8 from base\n7. Apply sign-extension: if value <= 0, set to -1; else keep value\n8. Enter main loop: test if slot value <= 0, exit if true (return 0)\n9. Increment slot index; if exceeds 13, branch to overflow handler\n10. Load slot base address from entity array using calculated offset\n11. If slot value != 0, dereference pointer and add value offset; else add 4-byte offset\n12. Load next slot value from +0x4; if > 0, loop to step 9\n13. On normal exit: return 0 (no overflow)\n14. On overflow: reset slot index to 0, call RehashEntityPool for cleanup, return 1\n\nParameters:\n  pEntityManager (ECX): Pointer to entity manager structure\n    +0x10: Current slot index (0-13, tracked during pool iteration)\n    +0x1C: Pointer to entity array/pool base address\n    +0x24: Entity pool mask (usage bitmap, 0x3FF = valid)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: 0 if processing succeeded normally, 1 if pool overflow occurred and cleanup was performed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Slot indices range from 0-13; overflow at 14+ triggers cleanup path\n  - Mask value 0x3FF (1023 in decimal) indicates saturated/valid state\n  - Slot values use sign-extension: non-positive values become -1 (all bits set)\n  - Pool traversal follows linked structure: each slot contains offset to next slot\n  - Overflow triggers RehashEntityPool for dynamic pool reorganization\n\nStructure Layout (Entity Manager):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n  +0x10    4    dwSlotIndex     dword     Current slot index for iteration (0-13)\n  +0x1C    4    pEntityArray    void*     Base address of entity pool storage\n  +0x24    4    dwPoolMask      dword     Entity mask/bitmap (0x3FF when valid)",
