      "name": "InitializeListNode",
      "signature": "void InitializeListNode(ListNode * pListNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes a doubly-linked list node structure with self-referential pointers and corruption detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract pListNode parameter from stack (ESP+0x10 after SEH prologue)\n2. Set up SEH exception frame with FS:[0] for safe exception handling\n3. Calculate pListNodeField pointer to offset +0x4 from base (LEA ECX,[EAX + 0x4])\n4. Zero all list node fields via pListNodeField: offset +0x0 and +0x4\n5. Initialize pListNodeField[0] to self-referential pointer: pListNodeField[0] = &pListNodeField\n6. Store bit-inverted pointer for integrity verification: pListNodeField[2] = ~(uint)pListNodeField\n7. Write sentinel value 0xdddddddd at pListNode[0] as uninitialized/error marker\n8. Re-initialize self-reference and inverted pointer to ensure consistency\n9. Mark exception state as complete (0xffffffff in ESP+0x8)\n10. Restore previous FS:[0] exception handler from SEH frame\n11. Clean up SEH frame (ADD ESP,0xc) and return with __stdcall cleanup (RET 0x4)\n\nParameters:\npListNode (ListNode *): Pointer to 12-byte list node structure to initialize\n  - Offset +0x0: dwType/sentinel field (written with 0xdddddddd)\n  - Offset +0x4: pSelfReference pointer (self-referential for linked list ops)\n  - Offset +0x8: dwInvertedPtr (bit-inverted pointer for corruption detection)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value. Function modifies the list node structure in place via pListNode parameter.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- SEH exception handling ensures cleanup on errors with FS:[0] frame management\n- Self-referential pointers enable doubly-linked list traversal operations\n- Bit-inverted pointer enables runtime corruption detection verification\n- Sentinel value 0xdddddddd marks uninitialized state for error detection\n- Double initialization pattern (steps 5-6 repeated at 8) ensures atomic/safe initialization\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention (callee cleanup, RET 0x4)\n- Called during object construction to initialize list linkage infrastructure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type     | Description\n0      | 4    | dwType           | uint     | Sentinel marker/type (0xdddddddd for uninitialized)\n4      | 4    | pSelfReference   | dword*   | Self-referential pointer for list traversal\n8      | 4    | dwInvertedPtr    | uint     | Bit-inverted copy of pSelfReference for validation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
