      "comment": "Resizes entity slot pool to match target allocation count.\n\nAdjusts the current slot allocation in a pooled entity structure to match a\ntarget size. If expanding, initializes new slots with list node structure.\nIf shrinking, cleans up removed slots. The function preserves the pool's\nlinked-list structure while reorganizing allocations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current slot count from pPoolManager[1] (+0x4)\n2. Load target slot count from EDI (implicit parameter in EDI register)\n3. Compare target with current:\n   a. If target > current (expansion path):\n      - Validate target does not exceed pool capacity at [ESI+0x0]\n      - If capacity not pre-allocated (pPoolManager[3]==0):\n        * Call CalculateNextValidCapacity to compute required capacity\n      - Calculate rounded allocation size using modulo arithmetic:\n        * EAX = target / capacity, EDX = remainder\n        * If remainder, round up: capacity = capacity - remainder + target\n      - Call ReallocateEntityPoolStorage to allocate new slots\n      - Loop from current to target, advancing by 0xc bytes per slot:\n        * Call InitializeListNodeWithSEH for each new slot\n      - Update pPoolManager[1] = target and return\n   b. If target < current (shrinking path):\n      - Loop from target to current, advancing by 0xc bytes per slot:\n        * Call ExecuteWithExceptionHandler at slot address for cleanup\n      - Update pPoolManager[1] = target and return\n   c. If target == current: Just update count and return\n\nParameters (Implicit):\n  EAX: pPoolManager\n    Pointer to entity pool manager (ArrayPool structure):\n    +0x0: uint    dwPoolCapacity    - Maximum entity count allowed\n    +0x4: uint    dwSlotCount       - Current active slot allocation count\n    +0x8: void*   pSlotArray        - Base pointer to entity slot array\n    +0xC: uint    dwAllocated       - Allocated capacity (0 if not set)\n  EDI: targetSlotCount\n    Target number of slots to resize pool to (expansion or shrinking)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value, modifies pool structure in place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Expansion uses 0xc-byte stride (12 bytes per slot = 3 dwords)\n  - Capacity rounding uses (size + modulo-1)/modulo approach\n  - Shrinking calls exception handlers for proper cleanup/destruction\n  - Expansion uses standard initialization handlers\n  - Magic offsets: 0x4=slot_count, 0x8=slot_array, 0xc=capacity field\n  - Calling convention: __d2call (implicit register parameters)\n\nStructure Layout (ArrayPool - 16 bytes total):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type     Description\n  ------  ----  ---------------   ----     --------------------------------\n  +0x0    4     dwPoolCapacity    uint     Max entity count\n  +0x4    4     dwSlotCount       uint     Current slot count\n  +0x8    4     pSlotArray        void*    Pointer to slot array\n  +0xC    4     dwAllocated       uint     Allocated capacity flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
