      "name": "InitializeGameObjectWithExceptionHandling",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameObjectWithExceptionHandling(void * pGameObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "InitializeGameObjectWithExceptionHandling - Safe game object initialization with Borland C++ exception handling\n\nSummary:\nSafely initializes a newly allocated game object by wrapping the initialization call with\nBorland C++ structured exception handling (SEH). Establishes an exception frame before calling\nthe actual initialization routine, ensuring proper cleanup and exception handler restoration\neven if an exception occurs during object setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current exception handler pointer from FS:[0x0] to pPreviousExceptionFrame\n2. Push exception frame components: sentinel (-1), return address (0x6fc32425), saved handler\n3. Set up new exception frame by pointing FS:[0x0] to ESP (stack-based frame)\n4. Initialize exception state marker to 0x0\n5. Load game object pointer parameter from stack (offset 0x10 relative to ESP)\n6. TEST the pointer to check if pGameObject is non-null\n7. If pGameObject is null, skip initialization (JZ skip_initialization_null_check)\n8. If non-null, PUSH pGameObject and CALL InitializeGameObjectFields(pGameObject)\n9. After call returns, write 0xffffffff to exception state cleanup marker\n10. Restore previous exception handler from stack into FS:[0x0]\n11. Clean up stack frame by adding 0xc bytes to ESP\n12. RET with 0x4 parameter cleanup (__stdcall convention)\n\nParameters:\npGameObject (EAX at entry, stack parameter): void* pointer to newly allocated game object\n  - Size: 0x60 bytes (96 bytes)\n  - Can be NULL: initialization safely skipped if null\n  - Passed from AllocateArraySlot after memory allocation\n  - Contains uninitialized memory for InitializeGameObjectFields to configure\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value, performs initialization side-effects only\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null object pointer: initialization safely skipped, no error reported\n- Exception during InitializeGameObjectFields: exception handler frame captures/re-throws\n- Exception handler restoration: guaranteed to run even if nested exception occurs\n- FS:[0x0] chain: Borland C++ maintains linked list of exception handlers via FS:[0x0]\n- Return address hardcoded: 0x6fc32425 points to Borland RTL exception handler entry\n- Stack sentinel: -1 (0xffffffff) marks exception frame boundary in linked list\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_pExceptionList (0xffdff000): Pointer to current exception handler frame in Borland C++ chain\n  - Saved at entry, restored at exit\n  - 303 cross-references across codebase for exception handling",
