      "name": "ExecuteCatchBlockHandler",
      "signature": "void * ExecuteCatchBlockHandler(EHRegistrationNode * pEhNode, _s_FuncInfo * pFuncInfo, void * pHandler, int nExceptionLevel, ulong nHandlerFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Sets up exception handling frame and executes the catch block handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load security cookie value (g_dwSecurityCookie) for stack overflow protection\n2. Copy function info pointer and increment exception level counter\n3. Set handler address pointer to pEHCatchBlockAddress for exception frame\n4. Store current exception registration node pointer\n5. Save current ExceptionList and install new local exception frame\n6. Call __CallSettingFrame_12 to execute the actual catch block handler with pHandler\n7. Restore previous exception list\n8. Return handler result (void pointer)\n\nParameters:\npEhNode: Pointer to EHRegistrationNode containing exception handling state\npFuncInfo: Pointer to _s_FuncInfo with function exception specification information\npHandler: Void pointer to the actual catch block handler function to execute\nnExceptionLevel: Current exception nesting level (incremented here for tracking depth)\nnHandlerFlags: Handler flags/options passed to __CallSettingFrame_12\n\nReturns:\nvoid*: Result from the catch block handler execution (may contain exception object or NULL)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Security cookie checked for stack buffer overflow detection\n- Exception list is temporarily modified to install frame-local handler\n- Handler nesting level is incremented to track exception depth\n- Stack frame setup follows Win32 x86 calling convention with EBP frame pointer\n\nStructure Layout:\nStack Frame (after PUSH EBP, SUB ESP, 0x18):\nOffset  Size  Field Name                Type      Description\n0x00    4     nExceptionLevelIncrement  int       nExceptionLevel + 1\n-0x04   4     pPreviousEhNode           void*     Copy of EHRegistrationNode pointer\n-0x08   4     pFuncInfoCopy             void*     Copy of function info pointer\n-0x0c   4     securityCheckValue        dword     Security cookie for overflow detection\n-0x10   4     pHandlerAddress           void*     Points to pEHCatchBlockAddress\n-0x14   4     pPreviousExceptionList    void*     Saves old ExceptionList for restoration",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
