      "name": "InvokeExceptionFrameDestructor",
      "signature": "void InvokeExceptionFrameDestructor(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Invokes exception frame destructor via stack-based exception handler wrapper.\nThis function serves as a thin wrapper for C++ exception unwinding, extracting\nan exception frame pointer from [EBP - 0x10] and passing it to the destructor\nhandler. Called during exception propagation to safely destroy exception objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load exception frame pointer from stack location [EBP - 0x10]\n2. Push exception frame pointer as parameter\n3. Call UnwindExceptionFrameDestructor to handle exception object destruction\n4. Return to caller (parameter cleanup via __stdcall)\n\nParameters:\n- Implicit: Exception frame pointer stored at [EBP - 0x10] before function entry\n\nReturns:\n- void: No explicit return value; this is an unwinding handler\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stack-based parameter: Parameter stored at [EBP - 0x10] rather than standard stack\n- Exception context: Function is called during C++ exception unwinding\n- Calling convention: __stdcall (callee cleanup)\n\nStructure Layout (Exception Frame, from UnwindExceptionFrameDestructor):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type      Description\n------  ----  -----------   --------  -----------\n0x0     4     reserved0     uint      Reserved/alignment\n0x4     4     reserved1     uint      Reserved/alignment\n0x8     4     pObject       void*     Pointer to object for destruction\n---     >=12  total size    struct    Exception frame minimum 12 bytes",
