      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleans up and unwinds an exception frame.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the exception frame pointer from the first parameter (passed via EBP+4)\n2. Add offset 0x28 to reach the cleanup structure within the frame\n3. Call CleanupExceptionFrame to perform the actual cleanup and exception unwinding\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionFrame: Pointer to the exception frame structure to unwind\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Performs cleanup as a side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This function serves as a wrapper/thunk that adjusts the pointer offset before calling the actual cleanup handler\n- Part of the C++ exception handling mechanism for exception frame cleanup\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe function accesses offset +0x28 within the exception frame, which points to a cleanup handler structure that is processed by CleanupExceptionFrame.",
