      "name": "UnwindFoundParamException",
      "signature": "void UnwindFoundParamException(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Unwinder for _FOUNDPARAM C++ exception type. Extracts handler callback from exception record\nand delegates to HandleFoundParamException for actual exception cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load exception record pointer from caller's stack frame (EBP + 4)\n2. Calculate exception handler address by adding offset 0x38 to the exception record base\n3. Push calculated handler address onto stack as parameter\n4. Call HandleFoundParamException to process the exception\n5. Return to caller (stdcall cleanup: RET 4 to remove 4-byte parameter)\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionRecord (void*): Pointer to exception record structure. The actual parameter\n    is accessed via stack frame pointer (EBP + 4). This is the callee's saved EBP from\n    the previous stack frame.\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value. Function returns via RET (stdcall convention).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Exception Offset: The constant 0x38 is a fixed offset into the exception record that\n    points to the handler callback pointer. This offset is specific to _FOUNDPARAM\n    exception structure layout in the C++ runtime.\n  \n  Stack Frame Access: The function accesses the caller's stack frame via the saved EBP\n    register (EBP + 4 contains the actual exception record pointer parameter).\n\nRelated Functions:\n  HandleFoundParamException: The actual exception handler that processes the unwinding.",
